 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones). I haven't run anything beyond that suite, so the new behaviour for the other SPEC sections is untested.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test for `None` counting as not converted (section 1) and one for the last duplicate id being kept (section 5).\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `conversions_in_window` entry now says the last `days` entries, and there is a new entry for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** Checking sections 8\u201310 turned up three more fixes:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and returns keys in sorted order.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` now counts only entries greater than 0.\n\nI also changed the README's `dedupe_sessions` line to describe what it now does.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made that raise `ValueError` with the `line N` message, like the other malformed lines.",
